                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "71802071",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198048659492",
                            "num_reviews": 231,
                            "playtime_forever": 425,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 425,
                            "last_played": 1592430112
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/30168383] If you liked the review and interested in completion and perfection time of games with additional useful information (for example: how difficult to get all achievements, is MP or DLC required and so on) or interested in reviews like this, then please follow my Average Achievement Hunter curator.               [/url]\n\nGreat Esport Manager is a clicker sim game. Wait, clicker, that is not even mentioned on the store page, it neither has that tag! Well, I finished the game and it felt like playing a clicker game.\n\nSo, what is the goal of this game? First of all, i believe, the main goal is to make you bored. No kidding! Repetitive tasks, boring memes and jokes and even more repetitive grind tasks.\n\nYou will play as an esport manager and you need to build up a pro gamer team. Each gamer has 4 different attribute skills, these represent 4 different game genres. You recruit gamers with low actual skills but much higher maximum skill limits. This is where the grind starts. You need to expand your building, implement furnitures/equpiments which increases their related skills. Move the characters to train on these skills, then move them to the bed so they get energy back. Training decreases ego so in the meantime you also need to move them to the computer so they can play online and get some ego. Too low or too high ego makes you lose that gamer permanently. You will keep repeating these tasks.\n\nBased on the activity of your gamers there are also 4 minigames. On these you just simply need to click on the right spot. This helps on skillboost while the gamer is on the training session or gives extra money if that minigame shows up while the computer(livestream) is being used.\n\nWhen your gamers are trained already you can send them to win cups. No, nothing will happen while they are there, they finish it in 2-3 mins and you will see the end result. You will just see the timer and once “mission done” they return. Like in a clicker game.\n\nOn big challenge cups, there are like 5-6 in the game, it is a bit different. The cup progress is based on the skills of your gamers but there are the already known clicker minigames that show up continuously and clicking correctly on them speed up the cup progress bar.\n\n[h1]Conclusion[/h1]\n\nDo not buy on full price, even on the highest ever -90% discount the game might be still expensive because of its boring clicky minigames and grind heavy, boring, repetitive content. You can buy much better games for your money.\n\nStory: 5/10, there are some jokes and memes in the game, some might like it, some not.\nReplay value: 1/10\nAtmosphere: 4/10\nVisuals: 6/10\nGameplay mechanics: 3/10, boring grindy content and simple clicker minigames\nMusic/Sound effects: 5/10\nGame difficulty: 2/10\n\n[h1]Hey, I am an achievement hunter![/h1]\nPerfection time: ~4-5h. Perfection is easy and could be done in a single playthrough. You just need to make sure you 3star every single location before going for the last challenge mission, which is located in North Korea.",
